  "summary": "On the night of 21 August 1986, a large release of carbon dioxide from volcanic Lake Nyos in Cameroon flowed down surrounding valleys and suffocated people and animals. EBSCO gives about 1,700 human deaths and 8,000 livestock; History.com says nearly 2,000 people died. Four villages were hit and buildings and plants were left unharmed.",
